From 0b216ee3737872917fcdb56197557e30eb04e89e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 05:22:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 146/147] hydra: the orthographic window is scaled by
 metersPerUnit

Everything sent to Cycles is in metres but the orthographic window was not:
on a stage without metersPerUnit (0.01 by USD's default) a 4-unit window
covered 400 units. bench_camera.py gains orthographic_cm. (K-107)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/hydra/camera.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/hydra/camera.cpp b/src/hydra/camera.cpp
index f61e898d..654bab89 100644
--- a/src/hydra/camera.cpp
+++ b/src/hydra/camera.cpp
@@ -234,6 +234,12 @@ void HdCyclesCamera::ApplyCameraSettings(HdRenderParam *renderParam,
 
     cam->set_fov(GfDegreesToRadians(data.GetFieldOfView(GfCamera::FOVVertical)));
   }
+  else {
+    /* An orthographic window is in scene units, like everything else sent
+     * to Cycles in metres: on a stage of centimetres it framed a hundred
+     * times too wide (K-107). */
+    viewplane *= metersPerUnit;
+  }
 
   cam->set_sensorwidth(data.GetHorizontalAperture() * GfCamera::APERTURE_UNIT * metersPerUnit);
   cam->set_sensorheight(data.GetVerticalAperture() * GfCamera::APERTURE_UNIT * metersPerUnit);
